.TH WIND_TUNNEL 1 "October 2026" "wind-tunnel-2d" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wind_tunnel \- 2D molecular-dynamics wind tunnel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wind_tunnel
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wind_tunnel
is a particle-based 2D wind tunnel. A gas of soft-repulsive discs is injected
from the left through a kinetic-flux boundary condition, flows through a
shaped channel past an obstacle, and exits on the right. Forces are
integrated with velocity-Verlet using a cell-list + Verlet neighbor list.
The particles are not true hard spheres but the WCA pseudo-hard-sphere
potential (Weeks-Chandler-Andersen), which has a well-defined speed of
sound and so a physically meaningful Mach number.
.PP
Reduced LJ units throughout:
.BR "sigma = m = epsilon = k_B = 1" .
Tunnel is 320 sigma long by 100 sigma tall.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B SPACE
Start/stop (start reseeds the gas).
.TP
.B P
Pause/resume.
.TP
.B V
Toggle MP4 recording (writes
.BR wind_tunnel_<timestamp>.mp4 ).
Requires
.B ffmpeg
on PATH.
.TP
.B R
Reset.
.TP
.B G
Cycle tunnel geometry (straight, de-Laval nozzle, venturi, diffuser,
transonic bump).
.TP
.B O
Cycle preset obstacle (none, cylinder, flat plate, wedge, NACA-0015 wing).
.TP
.B +\~/\~\(mi
Grow/shrink the preset obstacle.
.TP
.B 0
Reset preset obstacle to default size.
.TP
.B C
Clear all obstacles (preset and hand-placed).
.TP
.B [\~/\~]
Physics substeps per frame (1-40).
.TP
.B F
Flow-field view: particles -> field+particles -> field+arrows.
.TP
.B M
Render mode: points vs filled discs.
.TP
.B L
Toggle legend.
.TP
.B H
Toggle HUD.
.TP
.B Mouse
Wheel = zoom; right/middle-drag = pan; left-click = drop a circular
obstacle; left-drag on a slider = adjust it.
.TP
.B ESC, Q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Headless self-test mode (no window):
.TP
.B WT_SELFTEST=1
Run headless.
.TP
.B WT_STEPS
Number of steps (default 600).
.TP
.B "WT_GEOM WT_OBS WT_OBSCALE"
Geometry/obstacle preset and scale (integers; see README).
.TP
.B "WT_DENS WT_MACH WT_TEMP"
Density, Mach, temperature overrides.
.TP
.B "WT_ADDOBS_AT WT_ADDOBS"
Insert an obstacle at a given step (as the
.B O
key does).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Watch:
.PP
.RS
.B ./wind_tunnel
.RE
.PP
Headless cylinder stability check at Mach 2 (standing shock, should hold):
.PP
.RS
.B WT_SELFTEST=1 WT_GEOM=0 WT_OBS=1 WT_MACH=2.0 WT_STEPS=3000 ./wind_tunnel
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B wind_tunnel_<ISO-timestamp>.mp4
Written when
.B V
is pressed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lbm_tunnel (1),
.BR lbm_pro (1),
.BR lbm_bench (1)
.SH NOTES
True hard spheres require an event-driven scheduler (incompatible with
fixed-step integration); the WCA pseudo-hard-sphere model used here is
the standard MD resolution.
